Following yesterday's INC-260713 recovery, Checkout has reviewed the routing
telemetry and supports a guarded retry-ceiling update for Checkout SVC-17.

Proposed window: 15 Jul, 10:00-10:30 UTC.
Scope: apply the previous stable ceiling to the payment-routing client in the
two active regions, then observe checkout success rate and upstream saturation
for 20 minutes. The change is limited to configuration; no application build
is included.

Success criteria are a checkout success rate at or above 99.7%, no sustained
increase in 502 responses, and no additional draw beyond the current 2.4%
error budget. If either error signal rises for five consecutive minutes, Release
Coordination will revert the configuration and notify the incident thread.

Please confirm that the alert mute remains narrow to the routing symptom only.
The incident record should retain its resolved state unless the rollback is
needed.
